    "id": "registan",
    "cityId": "samarkand",
    "name": {
      "en": "Registan Square",
      "zh": "雷吉斯坦广场"
    },
    "category": "architecture",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "Three madrasahs facing one square — the image everyone has of the Silk Road.",
      "zh": "三座经学院共对一个广场——世人心中丝绸之路的标准画面。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Ulugh Beg built the first madrasah here between 1417 and 1420 as a school of astronomy and mathematics; two more were added two centuries later, each answering the last. The Sher-Dor facade breaks Islamic convention outright, with two tigers chasing deer beneath a human-faced sun. Go twice: around nine in the morning before the groups arrive, and again after dark when the facades are lit. Tickets are sold at the entrance and the queue doubles after ten.",
      "zh": "兀鲁伯于1417至1420年间在此建起第一座经学院，用作天文与数学学堂；两个世纪后又添两座，彼此呼应。希尔多经学院的正面公然突破了伊斯兰艺术的惯例——两只老虎追逐小鹿，头顶是一轮带人面的太阳。建议看两次：上午九点左右团队还没到，以及天黑后灯光亮起时。门票在入口处购买，十点以后排队时间会翻倍。"
    },
    "address": "Registan Street, Samarkand",
