  {
    "id": "gur-e-amir",
    "cityId": "samarkand",
    "name": {
      "en": "Gur-e-Amir Mausoleum",
      "zh": "古尔埃米尔陵（帖木儿陵）"
    },
    "category": "historical",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "Timur's tomb under a fluted turquoise dome, with a gold-leaf chamber inside.",
      "zh": "帖木儿长眠之处：青绿棱纹穹顶下，内室满铺金箔。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Timur built this for a grandson who died young, and ended up buried in it himself in 1405 under a slab of dark green jade. The ribbed dome is the shape every later Timurid architect copied, including the builders of the Taj Mahal. The interior is small and almost entirely gilded — twenty minutes is enough, but time it for late afternoon when light comes through the window grilles.",
      "zh": "帖木儿本是为早逝的孙子建造此陵，1405年他自己却葬在了这里，墓上覆着一整块墨绿玉石。那道棱纹穹顶成为后世帖木儿王朝建筑争相模仿的范式，泰姬陵的建造者也在其列。内部空间不大，几乎通体贴金——二十分钟足够，但最好安排在下午晚些时候，那时光线会从窗棂透进来。"
    },
    "address": "Bustonsaroy Street 2, Samarkand",
    "latitude": 39.6484,
    "longitude": 66.9689,
    "visitDuration": 60,
