  {
    "id": "shah-i-zinda",
    "cityId": "samarkand",
    "name": {
      "en": "Shah-i-Zinda",
      "zh": "沙赫静达陵墓群"
    },
    "category": "historical",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "An avenue of tombs climbing a hillside, tiled from floor to dome.",
      "zh": "沿山坡而上的陵墓长街，自地面到穹顶铺满琉璃。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Eleven mausoleums built over three centuries, packed shoulder to shoulder along a narrow lane and a flight of stairs. Because each family commissioned its own tomb, the tilework changes as you walk — carved terracotta, then majolica, then mosaic faience — so the street reads as a timeline of Central Asian ceramics. Come at opening time; the lane is too narrow to enjoy with crowds in it.",
      "zh": "十一座陵墓建于三个世纪之间，沿一条窄巷和一段台阶肩并肩排开。由于每座陵墓由不同家族出资，琉璃工艺随着你往上走而变化——先是雕花陶土，再是马约利卡彩陶，最后是马赛克镶嵌——整条街读起来就是一部中亚陶艺编年史。请在刚开门时来；巷子太窄，人多了就没法看了。"
    },
    "address": "Shahi Zinda Street, Samarkand",
