  {
    "id": "poi-kalyan",
    "cityId": "bukhara",
    "name": {
      "en": "Poi Kalyan Complex",
      "zh": "波依卡扬建筑群"
    },
    "category": "architecture",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "A 45-metre brick minaret from 1127 that Genghis Khan reportedly refused to destroy.",
      "zh": "1127年的45米砖砌宣礼塔，据说成吉思汗下令留它不毁。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The Kalyan minaret has stood since 1127 — fourteen bands of patterned brick, no two alike, tapering to a lantern about 46 metres up. It survived the Mongol sack of the city, the story goes, because Genghis Khan had to tip his head back to see the top and ordered it spared. The mosque on one side holds thousands of worshippers; the Mir-i-Arab madrasah opposite is still a working seminary and closed to visitors, so admire the facade from the square. Save this for late afternoon, when the brick turns gold.",
      "zh": "卡扬宣礼塔自1127年屹立至今——十四道纹样各异的砖砌腰带，向上收束，塔顶灯室高约46米。传说蒙古人洗劫全城时它得以幸存，是因为成吉思汗要仰头才能看见塔顶，于是下令保留。一侧的清真寺可容纳数千名礼拜者；对面的米里阿拉伯经学院至今仍是运作中的宗教学校，不对外开放，只能在广场上欣赏其立面。请留到下午晚些时候来，那时砖会变成金色。"
    },
    "address": "Hoja Nurobobod Street, Bukhara",
    "latitude": 39.7758,
    "longitude": 64.4142,
    "visitDuration": 90,
