  {
    "id": "samanid-mausoleum",
    "cityId": "bukhara",
    "name": {
      "en": "Samanid Mausoleum",
      "zh": "萨曼尼陵墓"
    },
    "category": "historical",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "The oldest building in Bukhara — a brick cube whose entire decoration is the bricks themselves.",
      "zh": "布哈拉最古老的建筑——一座立方体砖楼，全部装饰就是砖本身。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Built around the early 900s and buried under silt for centuries, which is why it survived the Mongols intact. There is no tile and no paint: the walls are woven from baked brick laid in basket patterns that change with the angle of the sun, so the building looks completely different at noon and at six in the evening. Small, perfect, and usually quiet.",
      "zh": "约建于十世纪初，此后数百年被泥沙掩埋，因而完整躲过了蒙古人的破坏。它没有琉璃，也没有彩绘：墙体由烧砖以编篮般的图案砌成，随太阳角度变化而变化，正午和傍晚六点看起来判若两座建筑。体量不大，却近乎完美，而且通常很安静。"
    },
    "address": "Samanid Park, Bukhara",
