  {
    "id": "trading-domes",
    "cityId": "bukhara",
    "name": {
      "en": "The Trading Domes",
      "zh": "商贸圆顶市场"
    },
    "category": "market",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "Domed medieval crossroads where money-changers, hat-makers and jewellers still trade.",
      "zh": "中世纪的穹顶十字路口，钱庄、帽匠与金匠至今仍在此营业。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Bukhara roofed over its main intersections in the sixteenth century so that trade could continue through the desert summer, and each dome specialised: caps in one, jewellers in another, money-changers in a third. Toqi Zargaron, the goldsmiths' dome, is the largest and best preserved. The specialisation mostly survives. Prices start high — expect to negotiate, and expect it to be friendly. This is the best place in the country to buy suzani embroidery and hand-forged knives.",
      "zh": "十六世纪，布哈拉给主要的十字路口加盖穹顶，使贸易在沙漠酷夏也能继续，每座穹顶各有专营：一座卖帽子，一座是金匠，还有一座是钱庄。金匠圆顶 Toqi Zargaron 规模最大、保存最好。这种行业分工大体保留至今。开价通常偏高——做好还价的准备，气氛是友好的。这里是全国购买苏扎尼刺绣和手工锻打刀具最好的地方。"
    },
