    },
    "category": "historical",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "The walled inner town — around fifty monuments inside a rectangle you can walk in twenty minutes.",
      "zh": "被城墙围起的内城——二十分钟能走穿的长方形里，藏着约五十处古迹。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "One combined ticket covers almost everything inside the walls and is valid for two days. The whole inner town is the UNESCO site rather than any single building in it, so the right way to see it is to start at the west gate, get the layout in your head from a high point, then wander without a plan. Around four hundred people still live inside, which is what stops it feeling like a museum.",
      "zh": "一张联票几乎涵盖城墙内所有景点，有效期两天。列入世界遗产的是整座内城，而不是其中某一座建筑，所以正确的看法是：从西门进入，先登高把布局记在脑子里，然后不按计划地随意走。城内至今仍住着约四百位居民，这正是它没有沦为博物馆的原因。"
    },
