    "name": {
      "en": "Kalta Minor Minaret",
      "zh": "卡尔塔米诺塔"
    },
    "category": "architecture",
    "shortDescription": {
      "en": "A fat, banded, fully glazed minaret abandoned at a third of its planned height.",
      "zh": "粗壮而通体琉璃的宣礼塔，停工时只建到计划高度的三分之一。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Muhammad Amin Khan wanted a tower tall enough to see Bukhara from. He died in 1855 with it around 29 metres up and 14 metres wide, and nobody continued the work — so Khiva ended up with a stump completely sheathed in glazed tile, which is far stranger and more memorable than the finished thing would have been. It sits just inside the west gate, so it is the first thing you meet.",
      "zh": "穆罕默德·阿明汗想建一座高到能望见布哈拉的塔。1855年他去世时，塔只砌到约29米高、直径14米，此后无人续建——于是希瓦得到了一截通体包覆琉璃砖的塔基，比建成的样子更奇特、也更令人难忘。它就在西门内侧，是你进城遇到的第一个建筑。"
    },
