    "description": {
      "en": "The khans' residence, mint, harem and summer mosque, built into the western wall of Ichan Kala from the seventeenth century onward. The summer mosque courtyard has the densest blue tilework in Khiva, and the watchtower at the corner is the climb to do first — from up there the whole walled town makes sense before you start walking it.",
      "zh": "这里是可汗的居所、铸币厂、后宫与夏用清真寺，自十七世纪起依托伊禅卡拉西城墙陆续建成。夏用清真寺庭院内的蓝色琉璃是希瓦最密集的，角上的瞭望塔则是最该先爬的地方——站上去以后，整座围城的格局一目了然，再开始走就清楚了。"
    },
