      "zh": "奥斯曼《古兰经》所在地，普遍认为是世上现存最古老的抄本之一。"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "The complex was largely rebuilt in 2007 around a set of older madrasahs, so the architecture is newer than it looks. The reason to come is in the library: a huge deerskin Quran attributed to the third caliph, Uthman, stained with what tradition holds is his blood. Photography is not allowed in that room. This is an active religious centre rather than a monument — dress modestly, and women should bring a headscarf.",
      "zh": "该建筑群于2007年围绕若干更早的经学院大规模重建，因此建筑比外表看上去要新。真正值得来的理由在图书馆：一部巨大的鹿皮《古兰经》，相传出自第三任哈里发奥斯曼之手，上面的痕迹据传是他的血。该展室禁止拍照。这里是仍在运作的宗教中心，而非单纯的古迹——请着装得体，女士请自备头巾。"
    },
